# Feature branches (required)

All changes happen on **`feature/*` branches** in git worktrees under `worktrees/`. **`main` is merge-only.**

## Before editing tracked files

1. Confirm `pwd` is under `worktrees/<name>/` (not the root working tree on `main`).
2. Confirm current branch matches `feature/*` (`git branch --show-current`).
3. If either check fails, create a worktree:

```bash
git worktree add worktrees/<name> -b feature/<name>
cd worktrees/<name>
```

## Commits

- Commit only from a `feature/*` branch inside `worktrees/`.
- `no-commit-to-branch` blocks commits to `main`; do not bypass except per project rules (`SKIP=no-commit-to-branch` only for `make check` on main).
- Merge to `main` locally after `make check` passes in the worktree (see `git-worktree-workflow.mdc`).

## Agents

Never implement, fix, or commit on `main`. Create or switch to a feature worktree first.
